14
00:00:54,838 --> 00:00:57,838
For some reason they were nicknamed memory holes.

15
00:00:57,838 --> 00:01:02,159
When one knew that any document was due for destruction, or even when one saw a

16
00:01:02,159 --> 00:01:06,479
scrap of waste paper lying about, it was an automatic action to lift the flap of

17
00:01:06,479 --> 00:01:11,338
the nearest memory hole and drop it in whereuponnet would be whirled away on a

18
00:01:11,338 --> 00:01:15,060
current of warm air to the enormous furnaces which were hidden somewhere in

19
00:01:15,060 --> 00:01:18,119
the recesses of the building.

20
00:01:18,119 --> 00:01:22,979
Winston examined the four slips of paper which he had unrolled. Each contained a

21
00:01:22,979 --> 00:01:27,479
message of only one or two lines, in the abbreviated jargon— —not actually news

22
00:01:27,479 --> 00:01:32,340
speak but consisting largely of Newspeak words— —which was used in the Ministry for

23
00:01:32,340 --> 00:01:33,960
internal purposes.

24
00:01:33,960 --> 00:01:41,039
They ran: times 17 384 bb speech male reported africa rectify

25
00:01:41,039 --> 00:01:48,420
times 19 1283 forecasts 3yp 4th quarter 83 misprints verify current issue

26
00:01:48,420 --> 00:01:57,899
times 14 to 84 mini plenty malquoted chocolate rectify times 3 1283 reporting bb day order

27
00:01:57,899 --> 00:02:04,859
double plus ungood riffs on Persons rewrite full wise up sub anti-filing

28
00:02:04,859 --> 00:02:09,359
With a faint feeling of satisfaction Winston laid the fourth message aside.

29
00:02:09,359 --> 00:02:13,738
It was an intricate and responsible job and had better be dealt with last.

30
00:02:13,738 --> 00:02:17,219
The other three were routine matters, though the second one would probably

31
00:02:17,219 --> 00:02:20,960
mean some tedious waiting through lists of figures.

32
00:02:20,960 --> 00:02:24,779
Winston dialed back numbers' on the telescreen and called for the

33
00:02:24,779 --> 00:02:28,619
