35
00:02:30,658 --> 00:02:35,100
The messages he had received referred to articles or news items which for one

36
00:02:35,100 --> 00:02:38,640
reason or another it was thought necessary to alter, or, as the official

37
00:02:38,640 --> 00:02:41,279
phrase had it, to rectify.

38
00:02:41,279 --> 00:02:45,960
For example, it appeared from the Times of the 17th of March that Big Brother, in

39
00:02:45,960 --> 00:02:49,560
his speech of the previous day, had predicted that the South Indian front

40
00:02:49,560 --> 00:02:55,319
would remain quiet but that the Eurasian offensive would shortly be launched in North Africa.

41
00:02:55,319 --> 00:02:58,979
As it happened the Eurasian Higher Command had launched its offensive in

42
00:02:58,979 --> 00:03:01,979
South India and left North Africa alone.

43
00:03:01,979 --> 00:03:06,238
It was therefore necessary to rewrite a paragraph of Big Brother's speech, in

44
00:03:06,238 --> 00:03:09,719
such a way as to make him predict the thing that had actually happened.

45
00:03:09,719 --> 00:03:14,158
Or again, the Times of the 19th of December had published the official

46
00:03:14,158 --> 00:03:18,179
forecasts of the output of various classes of consumption goods in the

47
00:03:18,179 --> 00:03:24,300
fourth quarter of 1983,. which was also the sixth quarter of the Ninth Three-Year Plan.

48
00:03:24,300 --> 00:03:28,260
Today's issue contained a statement of the actual output, from which it appeared

49
00:03:28,260 --> 00:03:31,500
that the forecasts were in every instance grossly wrong.

50
00:03:31,500 --> 00:03:36,539
Winston's job was to rectify the original figures by making them agree with the later ones.

51
00:03:36,539 --> 00:03:40,619
As for the third message, it referred to a very simple error which could be set

52
00:03:40,619 --> 00:03:45,119
right in a couple of minutes a shorter time ago as February, the

53
00:03:45,119 --> 00:03:49,020
Ministry of Plenty had issued a promise (a 'categorical pledge with the official

54
00:03:49,020 --> 00:03:53,698
words) that there would be no reduction of the chocolate ration during 1984..

55
00:03:53,698 --> 00:03:57,899
Actually, as Winston was aware, the chocolate ration was to be reduced from

56
00:03:57,899 --> 00:04:01,020
30 grams to 20 at the end of the present week.

57
00:04:01,020 --> 00:04:05,039
All that was needed was to substitute for the original promise a warning that

58
00:04:05,039 --> 00:04:09,000
it would probably be necessary to reduce the ration at some time in April

59
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:13,738
foreign As soon as Winston had dealt with each of the messages, he clipped his

60
00:04:13,738 --> 00:04:17,340
speak written corrections to the appropriate copy of the Times and pushed

61
00:04:17,340 --> 00:04:19,260
them into the pneumatic tube.

62
00:04:19,260 --> 00:04:23,579
Then, with a movement which was nearly as possible unconscious, he crumpled up the

63
00:04:23,579 --> 00:04:27,420
original message and any notes that he himself had made, and dropped them into

64
00:04:27,420 --> 00:04:31,760
the memory hole to be devoured by the flames.

65
00:04:31,859 --> 00:04:36,060
What happened in the unseen labyrinth to which the pneumatic tubes led, he did not

66
00:04:36,060 --> 00:04:39,300
know in detail, but he did know in general terms.

67
00:04:39,300 --> 00:04:42,479
As soon as all the corrections which happened to be necessary in any

68
00:04:42,479 --> 00:04:46,738
particular number of the Times had been assembled and collated, that number would

69
00:04:46,738 --> 00:04:51,060
be reprinted, the original copy destroyed, and the corrected copy placed on the

70
00:04:51,060 --> 00:04:52,679
files in its stead.

71
00:04:52,679 --> 00:04:57,000
This process of continuous alteration was applied not only to newspapers, but

72
00:04:57,000 --> 00:05:02,939
to books, periodicals, pamphlets, posters, leaflets, films, soundtracks, cartoons,

73
00:05:02,939 --> 00:05:07,738
photographs— —to every kind of literature or documentation which might conceivably

74
00:05:07,738 --> 00:05:11,219
hold any political or ideological significance.

75
00:05:11,219 --> 00:05:15,840
Day by day and almost minute by minute the past was brought up to date.

76
00:05:15,840 --> 00:05:19,439
In this way every prediction made by the Party could be shown by documentary

77
00:05:19,439 --> 00:05:24,000
evidence to have been correct; nor was any item of news, or any expression of

78
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:29,219
opinion, which conflicted with the needs of the moment, ever allowed to remain on record.

79
00:05:29,219 --> 00:05:36,060
All history was a palimpsest, scraped clean and re-inscribed exactly as often as was necessary.

80
00:05:36,060 --> 00:05:40,079
In no case would it have been possible, once the deed was done, to prove that any

81
00:05:40,079 --> 00:05:42,179
falsification had taken place.

82
00:05:42,179 --> 00:05:46,319
The largest section of the Records Department, far larger than the one on

83
00:05:46,319 --> 00:05:50,640
which Winston worked, consisted simply of persons whose duty it was to track down

84
00:05:50,640 --> 00:05:54,600
and collect all copies of books, newspapers and other documents which had

85
00:05:54,600 --> 00:05:57,600
been superseded and were due for destruction.

86
00:05:57,600 --> 00:06:01,020
A number of the Times which might, because of changes in political

87
00:06:01,020 --> 00:06:06,000
alignment, or mistaken prophecies uttered by Big Brother, have been rewritten a

88
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:10,198
dozen times still stood on the files bearing its original date, and no other

89
00:06:10,198 --> 00:06:12,779
copy existed to contradict it.

90
00:06:12,779 --> 00:06:17,340
Books, also, were recalled and Rewritten again and again, and were invariably

91
00:06:17,340 --> 00:06:21,119
reissued without any admission that any alteration had been made.

92
00:06:21,119 --> 00:06:25,260
Even the written instructions which Winston received, and which he invariably

93
00:06:25,260 --> 00:06:29,219
got rid of as soon as he had dealt with them, never stated or implied that an act

94
00:06:29,219 --> 00:06:34,439
of forgery was to be committed: always the reference was to slips, errors,

95
00:06:34,439 --> 00:06:40,738
misprints or misquotations which it was necessary to put right in the interests of accuracy.

96
00:06:40,738 --> 00:06:45,119
But actually, he thought as he readjusted the Ministry of Plenty's figures, it was

97
00:06:45,119 --> 00:06:50,279
not even forgery. It was merely the substitution of one piece of nonsense for another.

98
00:06:50,279 --> 00:06:53,760
Most of the material that you were dealing with had no connection with

99
00:06:53,760 --> 00:06:58,920
anything in the real world, not even the kind of connection that is contained in a direct lie.

100
00:06:58,920 --> 00:07:04,140
Statistics were just as much a fantasy in their original version as in their rectified version.

101
00:07:04,140 --> 00:07:07,979
A great deal of the time you were expected to make them up out of your head.

102
00:07:07,979 --> 00:07:11,698
For example, the Ministry of Plenty's forecast had estimated the output of

103
00:07:11,698 --> 00:07:16,079
boots for the quarter at 145 million pairs.

104
00:07:16,079 --> 00:07:19,738
The actual output was given as 62 millions.

105
00:07:19,738 --> 00:07:24,359
Winston, however, in rewriting the forecast, marked the figure down to 57

106
00:07:24,359 --> 00:07:29,819
millions, so as to allow for the usual claim that the quota had been over fulfilled

107
00:07:29,819 --> 00:07:35,760
In any case 62 millions was no nearer the truth than 57 millions more than 145

108
00:07:35,760 --> 00:07:39,899
millions. Very likely no boots had been produced at all

109
00:07:39,899 --> 00:07:44,219
likely as still, nobody knew how many had been produced, much less cared.

110
00:07:44,219 --> 00:07:48,119
All one knew was that every quarter astronomical numbers of boots were

111
00:07:48,119 --> 00:07:53,219
produced on paper, while perhaps half the population of Oceania went barefoot.

112
00:07:53,219 --> 00:07:57,060
And so it was with every class of recorded fact, great or small.

113
00:07:57,060 --> 00:08:01,560
Everything faded away into a shadow World in which, finally, even the date of

114
00:08:01,560 --> 00:08:04,760
the year had become uncertain.

115
00:08:04,760 --> 00:08:09,539
Winston glanced across the hall. In the corresponding cubicle on the other side

116
00:08:09,539 --> 00:08:14,460
a small precise looking dark chinned man named Tillotson was working steadily

117
00:08:14,460 --> 00:08:18,420
away, with a folded newspaper on his knee and his mouth very close to the

118
00:08:18,420 --> 00:08:22,619
mouthpiece of the speak right He had the air of trying to keep what he

119
00:08:22,619 --> 00:08:25,859
was saying a secret between himself and the telescreen.

120
00:08:25,859 --> 00:08:31,399
He looked up, and his spectacles started a hostile flash in Winston's direction.

121
00:08:31,399 --> 00:08:36,300
Winston hardly knew Tillerson and had no idea what work he was employed on.

122
00:08:36,300 --> 00:08:40,619
People in the Records Department did not readily talk about their jobs.

123
00:08:40,619 --> 00:08:44,880
In the long, windowless hall, with its double row of cubicles and its endless

124
00:08:44,880 --> 00:08:48,960
rustle of papers and hum of voices murmuring into speak rights there were

125
00:08:48,960 --> 00:08:52,560
quite a dozen people whom Winston did not even know by name, though he daily

126
00:08:52,560 --> 00:08:58,319
saw them hurrying to and fro in the corridors or gesticulating in the Two Minutes Hate.

127
00:08:58,319 --> 00:09:02,340
He knew that in the cubicle next to him the little woman with sandy hair toiled

128
00:09:02,340 --> 00:09:06,840
day in, day out, simply it's tracking down into deleting from the press the names

129
00:09:06,840 --> 00:09:12,179
of people who had been vaporized and were therefore considered never to have existed.

130
00:09:12,179 --> 00:09:16,079
There was a certain fitness in this, since her own husband had been vaporized

131
00:09:16,079 --> 00:09:20,460
a couple of years earlier a few cubicles away a mild, ineffectual,

132
00:09:20,460 --> 00:09:25,198
dreamy creature named appleforth with very hairy ears and a surprising talent

133
00:09:25,198 --> 00:09:29,600
for juggling with rhymes and meters was engaged in producing garbled diversions

134
00:09:29,600 --> 00:09:34,319
definitive texts, they were called— —of poems which had become ideologically

135
00:09:34,319 --> 00:09:39,600
offensive but which for one reason or another were to be retained in the anthologies.

136
00:09:39,600 --> 00:09:44,579
And this hall, with its 50 workers or thereabouts, was only one subsection a

137
00:09:44,579 --> 00:09:48,779
single cell, as it were, in the huge complexity of the Records Department.

138
00:09:48,779 --> 00:09:56,460
Beyond, above, below where other swarms of workers engaged in an unimaginable multitude of jobs.

139
00:09:56,460 --> 00:10:00,359
There was a huge printing shops with their sub-editors, their typography

140
00:10:00,359 --> 00:10:05,520
experts and their elaborately equipped studios for the faking of photographs.

141
00:10:05,520 --> 00:10:09,719
There was the teller programs section with its engineers, its producers and its

142
00:10:09,719 --> 00:10:14,100
teams of actors specially chosen for their skill in imitating voices.

143
00:10:14,100 --> 00:10:17,399
There were the armies of reference clerks whose job was simply to draw up

144
00:10:17,399 --> 00:10:21,359
lists of books and periodicals which were due for recall.

145
00:10:21,359 --> 00:10:25,500
There were the vast repositories where the corrected documents were stored, and

146
00:10:25,500 --> 00:10:28,859
the hidden furnaces where the original copies were destroyed.

147
00:10:28,859 --> 00:10:33,000
And somewhere or other, quite anonymous, there were the directing brains who

148
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:37,020
coordinated the whole effort and laid down the lines of policy which made it

149
00:10:37,020 --> 00:10:40,859
necessary that this fragment of the past should be preserved, that one falsified,

150
00:10:40,859 --> 00:10:44,779
and the other rubbed out of existence.

151
00:10:44,819 --> 00:10:48,479
And the Records Department, after all, was itself only a single branch of the

152
00:10:48,479 --> 00:10:53,039
Ministry of Truth, whose primary job was not to reconstruct the past but to

153
00:10:53,039 --> 00:10:57,840
supply the citizens of Oceania with newspapers, films, textbooks, telescreen

154
00:10:57,840 --> 00:11:01,679
programs plays, novels— with every conceivable kind of information,

155
00:11:01,679 --> 00:11:06,779
instruction or entertainment, from a statue to a slogan, from a lyric poem to

156
00:11:06,779 --> 00:11:12,179
a biological treatise, and from a child's spelling book to a Newspeak dictionary.

157
00:11:12,179 --> 00:11:16,800
And the Ministry had not only to supply the multifarious needs of the Party, but

158
00:11:16,800 --> 00:11:21,600
also to repeat the whole operation at a lower level for the benefit of the proletariat.

159
00:11:21,600 --> 00:11:25,020
There was a whole chain of separate departments dealing with proletarian

160
00:11:25,020 --> 00:11:28,979
literature, music, drama and entertainment generally.

161
00:11:28,979 --> 00:11:33,000
Here were produced rubbish newspapers containing almost nothing except sport,

162
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:39,300
crime and astrology, sensational five cent novelets films oozing with sex, and

163
00:11:39,300 --> 00:11:42,899
sentimental songs which were composed entirely by mechanical means on a

164
00:11:42,899 --> 00:11:46,380
special kind of kaleidoscope known as a versificator.

165
00:11:46,380 --> 00:11:51,779
There was even a whole subsection porno second was called in Newspeak— —engaged in

166
00:11:51,779 --> 00:11:56,158
producing the lowest kind of pornography, which was sent out in sealed packets and

167
00:11:56,158 --> 00:12:01,859
which no Party member, other than those who worked on it, was permitted to look at.

168
00:12:01,859 --> 00:12:05,279
Three messages had slid out of the pneumatic tube while Winston was working;

169
00:12:05,279 --> 00:12:09,000
but they were simple matters, and he had disposed of them before the Two Minutes

170
00:12:09,000 --> 00:12:10,979
Hate interrupted him.

171
00:12:10,979 --> 00:12:15,238
When the Hate was over he returned to his cubicle, took the Newspeak dictionary

172
00:12:15,238 --> 00:12:19,800
from the shelf, pushed the speak writer to one side, cleaned his spectacles and

173
00:12:19,800 --> 00:12:22,738
settled down to his main job of the morning.

174
00:12:22,738 --> 00:12:27,238
Winston's greatest pleasure in life was in his work. Most of it was a tedious

175
00:12:27,238 --> 00:12:30,899
routine, but included in it there were also jobs so difficult and intricate

176
00:12:30,899 --> 00:12:34,698
that you could lose yourself in them as in the depths of a mathematical problem—

177
00:12:34,698 --> 00:12:38,579
—delicate pieces of forgery in which you had nothing to guide you except your

178
00:12:38,579 --> 00:12:43,738
knowledge of the principles of insock and your estimate of what the Party wanted you to say.

179
00:12:43,738 --> 00:12:46,140
Winston was good at this kind of thing.

180
00:12:46,140 --> 00:12:49,679
On occasion he had even been entrusted with the rectification of the Times

181
00:12:49,679 --> 00:12:54,539
leading articles, which were written entirely in Newspeak. He unrolled the

182
00:12:54,539 --> 00:13:01,679
message that he had set aside earlier. It ran: times 3 1283 reporting bb day order

183
00:13:01,679 --> 00:13:07,800
double plus ungood riffs unpersons rewrite full wise up sub anti-filing

184
00:13:07,800 --> 00:13:12,119
In Old speak or Standard English) this might be rendered:

185
00:13:12,119 --> 00:13:16,140
The reporting of Big Brother's Order for the Day in the Times of December the 3rd

186
00:13:16,140 --> 00:13:21,539
1983 is extremely unsatisfactory and makes references to non-existent persons

187
00:13:21,539 --> 00:13:26,939
rewrite it in full and submit your draft to higher authority before filing.

188
00:13:26,939 --> 00:13:29,819
Winston read through the offending article.

189
00:13:29,819 --> 00:13:33,119
Big Brother's Order for the Day, it seemed, had been chiefly devoted to

190
00:13:33,119 --> 00:13:37,859
praising the work of an organization known as FFCC, which supplied cigarettes

191
00:13:37,859 --> 00:13:41,039
and other comforts to the sailors in the Floating Fortresses.

192
00:13:41,039 --> 00:13:45,658
A certain Comrade Withers, a prominent member of the Inner Party, had been

193
00:13:45,658 --> 00:13:49,619
singled out for special mention and awarded a decoration, the Order of

194
00:13:49,619 --> 00:13:52,800
Conspicuous Merit, Second Class.

195
00:13:52,800 --> 00:13:57,658
Three months later FFCC had suddenly been dissolved with no reasons given.

196
00:13:57,658 --> 00:14:01,319
One could assume that Withers and his associates were now in disgrace, but

197
00:14:01,319 --> 00:14:04,859
there had been no report of the matter in the press or on the telescreen.

198
00:14:04,859 --> 00:14:08,760
That was to be expected, since it was unusual for political offenders to be

199
00:14:08,760 --> 00:14:11,279
put on trial or even publicly denounced.

200
00:14:11,279 --> 00:14:15,600
The great purges involving thousands of people, with public trials of traitors

201
00:14:15,600 --> 00:14:18,899
and thought criminals who made abject confession of their crimes and were

202
00:14:18,899 --> 00:14:25,140
afterwards executed with special showpieces not occurring often than once in a couple of years.

203
00:14:25,140 --> 00:14:29,039
More commonly, people who had incurred the displeasure of the Party simply

204
00:14:29,039 --> 00:14:31,859
disappeared and were never heard of again.

205
00:14:31,859 --> 00:14:35,399
One never had the smallest clue as to what had happened to them.

206
00:14:35,399 --> 00:14:38,158
In some cases they might not even be dead.

207
00:14:38,158 --> 00:14:42,600
Perhaps 30 people personally known to Winston, not counting his parents, had

208
00:14:42,600 --> 00:14:45,960
disappeared at one time or another.

209
00:14:45,960 --> 00:14:51,238
Winston stroked his nose gently with a paperclip In the cubicle across the way Comrade

210
00:14:51,238 --> 00:14:54,779
Tillerson was still crouching secretively over his speak right

211
00:14:54,779 --> 00:14:59,039
He raised his head for a moment: again the hostile spectacle Flash

212
00:14:59,039 --> 00:15:02,640
Winston wondered whether Comrade Tillerson was engaged on the same job as

213
00:15:02,640 --> 00:15:05,460
himself. It was perfectly possible.

214
00:15:05,460 --> 00:15:09,719
So tricky a piece of work would never be entrusted to a single person: on the

215
00:15:09,719 --> 00:15:13,020
other hand, to turn it over to a committee would be to admit openly that

216
00:15:13,020 --> 00:15:15,840
an act of fabrication was taking place.

217
00:15:15,840 --> 00:15:19,439
Very likely as many as a dozen people were now working away on rival versions

218
00:15:19,439 --> 00:15:21,960
of what Big Brother had actually said.

219
00:15:21,960 --> 00:15:26,399
And presently some master brain in the Inner Party would select this version or

220
00:15:26,399 --> 00:15:30,539
that, would re-edit it and set in motion the complex processes of

221
00:15:30,539 --> 00:15:34,800
cross-referencing that would be required, and then the chosen lie would pass into

